    "title": "Anthropic's run-rate revenue hits $47 billion",
    "summary": "<p>The most interesting thing about <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/series-h\">Anthropic's $65B Series H announcement</a> is this line (emphasis mine):</p> <blockquote> <p>Since our Series G in February, adoption has continued to grow across global enterprise customers, and our run-rate revenue crossed <strong>$47 billion</strong> earlier this month.</p> </blockquote> <p>Anthropic have made a bit of a habit of sharing their \"run-rate revenue\" in this kind of announcement, which is an annualized projection of their current revenue - typically calculated by taking the most recent month and multiplying by 12.</p> <p>Earlier this year:</p> <ul> <li>Apr 6, 2026 in <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/google-broadcom-partnership-compute\">Anthropic expands partnership with Google and...",
